# CSE476 configuration.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in ONE lane. You do not need all four.
#   cp .env.example .env          (macOS / Linux)
#   copy .env.example .env        (Windows)
#
# NEVER commit .env. It is already in .gitignore. Keep it that way.

# Which lane to use: foundry | github | groq | local
PROVIDER=github

# Optional. Overrides the lane's default model.
# MODEL=

# --- Lane B, GitHub Models. Free. This is the course default. -----------
# Create at github.com/settings/tokens
# A classic token with NO scopes ticked is enough.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Lane A, Microsoft Foundry. Needs an Azure subscription. ------------
# Formerly called Azure AI Foundry. Renamed January 2026.
# The endpoint must be the v1 base, ending in /openai/v1/.
# Get it from the Foundry portal: your deployment > the key icon > Endpoint.
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://your-resource.openai.azure.com/openai/v1/
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# For this lane, MODEL must be your DEPLOYMENT name, not the model name.
# You deployed a model and named the deployment 'chat-demo', so MODEL=chat-demo.

# --- Lane C, Groq. Free tier, reduced limits since 2026. ----------------
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- Lane D, Ollama on your own machine. No key needed. -----------------
# Install from ollama.com, then:  ollama pull llama3.2
